      "content": "The exhaustion you feel is real, and it's okay to feel completely depleted right now. When everything feels like a void, the pressure to \"perform\" or \"try\" is immense, so please stop fighting the urge to just rest. If the effort feels too heavy, focusing on the absolute smallest things—like just letting yourself be still—is a valid form of survival. Reaching out to a crisis line can offer immediate, non-judgmental support when the weight of everything feels too much to bear.",
